    title: "Is UK's Storm Shadow missile a game changer for Ukraine?",
    summary: "Correspondent Joe Inwood breaks down the weapons technology that could make a difference in the Russia-Ukraine war.",
    preview: "The UK has handed secret blueprints to Ukraine that will allow the country to build its own long-range cruise missiles. The announcement came during Andy Burnham's first visit to Kyiv as prime minster, where he met Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky. But faced with an almost daily barrage of Russian ballistic missiles, correspondent Joe Inwood explains why the offer may not be enough to win the war. Related topics - War in UkraineUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
    body: "The UK has handed secret blueprints to Ukraine that will allow the country to build its own long-range cruise missiles.\n\nThe announcement came during Andy Burnham's first visit to Kyiv as prime minster, where he met Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky.\n\nBut faced with an almost daily barrage of Russian ballistic missiles, correspondent Joe Inwood explains why the offer may not be enough to win the war.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- War in UkraineUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- UkraineUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- RussiaUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Volodymyr ZelenskyUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
